    one that's expensive to undo, because it introduces a module and a call convention other code will follow.

  [1mMy recommendation: login derives it.[0m Your goal is knowing [3mwho[0m logged in, and the only party that can authoritatively
  answer that is the thing doing the authenticating. Threading a [38;5;153muserId[39m in from a caller that doesn't have one means
  fabricating an identity source to satisfy a parameter.
